  "description": "Breaded, melty cheese is something that crosses cultures—from deep-fried mozzarella sticks to Latin American queso frito. Here, we've taken breaded squares of cheese and \"fried\" them in the waffle iron until their outsides turn golden brown and crunchy and their insides are melted and gooey.",
  "notes": "Optional or for serving: Salsa, for serving (optional)\n\nNotes: Any good melting cheese such as young provolone, fontina, Jack, cheddar, or a queso chihuahua can be used in place of the mozzarella. Avoid fresh mozzarella or dry cheese meant for grating. Some recipes call for the breaded cheese to be refrigerated (or frozen) before cooking. I did not find this to be necessary with the waffle iron version, but you can certainly bread the cheese several hours ahead and refrigerate it until you're ready to waffle.",
  "author": [
    "Daniel Shumski"
  ],
